{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/115771-true-faith-seeking","id":115771,"title":"True Faith Seeking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-19T03:49:48-07:00","id":115771,"title":"True Faith Seeking","content":"True Faith may not be raised with Experience. It must be raised via shows of dedication to the Faith.<br /> How do you, as storytellers, run this?<br /> For an example: assume for a Christian character who only has True Faith 1, who is not an Inquisitor or the like, but rather a Mage or Vampire, and little to no access to other people who have True Faith scores (because it is rare as heck). How would you get this character to True Faith 2?<br /> (Statements of: not allowing True Faith; not allowing it on supernaturals; or not allowing it to be increased, are not constructive.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T07:49:34-07:00","id":115851,"title":"","content":"Depends on the base system you are using. In the new Hunter's Hunted II book, True Faith now functions like any other Numina, being raised with experience. I'm not sure I really like that personally though. I always liked True Faith being something more than other powers, functioning differently. Before that book, it was very subjective for me. I would run through various quests and judge their behavior on the harshest of terms to see if they were worthy. I'd let them raise their True Faith when they performed either some big grand act of phenomenal faith, or when the accumulation of small acts was so overwhelming it merited it in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T08:45:47-07:00","id":115896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/115771-true-faith-seeking?p=115851#post115851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the base system you are using.</div> </div> </div> </div>System is that of either Vampire, or Mage. Revised edition, FWIW.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/115771-true-faith-seeking?p=115851#post115851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would run through various quests and judge their behavior on the harshest of terms to see if they were worthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is likewise how I handle a Mages Seekings, which is why I titled the thread what I did.<br /> Can you give some examples of yours?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/115771-true-faith-seeking?p=115851#post115851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd let them raise their True Faith when they performed either some big grand act of phenomenal faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/115771-true-faith-seeking?p=115851#post115851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd let them raise their True Faith when the accumulation of small acts was so overwhelming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as?<br /> How much above just being a decent person do you need to go for this 'small act' do you need to go?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T12:33:21-07:00","id":116031,"title":"","content":"True Faith is really hard to quantify. I see it as an innately personal thing. Whenever I have someone who wants to go for True Faith (I don't usually let any player start with it, but I'm open to them earning it in game), I have a long chat with them about the details of their Faith and what do they believe in (broad terms of what religion all the way to individual details of how they view each aspect of it). I tend to work with them to form a faith paradigm not unlike a Path of Enlightenment with tenets and sins. When they have done enough in keeping with the tenets (usually requiring either a long time just following the tenets or some very large act such as a personal sacrifice for their faith) I will give them a dot of True Faith. They have to live basically without sin or if their paradigm allows, always atoning for any sin. <br /> <br /> As for small acts, I tend to really disagree with the book saying that the Pope has True Faith 4+. I think that where you find True Faith is not in the high offices of the church or other large religions. They are politicians far more than true holy men. I think you find the high levels of true faith in forgotten monasteries where you have the old monk who has truly given up his life for his faith. In keeping with that, I see the value of each act usually in terms of how great a personal sacrifice it is, how much the individual is putting their faith before temporal concerns. <br /> <br /> It's hard to explain and I don't have an organized system. I must admit that a lot of it is gut instinct as an ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T15:36:28-07:00","id":279130,"title":"","content":"True Faith is something that never came up in my games before save for NPCs, but I'm running a game with a Chorister character who asked about this Trait and got me thinking. I was reading the rules on True Faith on the Mage the Ascension Revised core and Celestial Choruls Revised Trad books. Then I googled &quot;raising True Faith&quot; and found this thread. I find the idea of running Seeking-like scenarios to reaise Faith an interesting one, but I have no specific ideas, so if any come up, I'd be interested. Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3144-viradu","name":"Viradu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T16:46:16-07:00","id":279164,"title":"","content":"Seekings from M:tA or Moments of Truth from DA:V would seem the most reasonable parts to take inspiration from, if you ask me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T02:53:59-07:00","id":279474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/115771-true-faith-seeking?p=116031#post116031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to really disagree with the book saying that the Pope has True Faith 4+. I think that where you find True Faith is not in the high offices of the church or other large religions. They are politicians far more than true holy men.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree about the forgotten monks in their monasteries I disagree about Pope while agreeing with your assessment of his personal faith and him being more politician than a holy man. What I mean is that I think Pope has True Faith 4+ in exactly the same manner that a Church can have True Faith score, he is the focus point of millions of believers from all over hte world and as such kinda carries with him a sort of passive score of True Faith.<br /> <br /> Naturally YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T10:50:52-07:00","id":279887,"title":"","content":"I love True Faith, it's one of my favorite merits. To increase it I would prefer that the PC be put in contact with something that challenges their faith. Made it through, even and especially when it was dangerous to hold to your convictions? Cool, have a faith cookie and level up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T12:44:19-07:00","id":280020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/115771-true-faith-seeking?p=279474#post279474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree about the forgotten monks in their monasteries I disagree about Pope while agreeing with your assessment of his personal faith and him being more politician than a holy man. What I mean is that I think Pope has True Faith 4+ in exactly the same manner that a Church can have True Faith score, he is the focus point of millions of believers from all over hte world and as such kinda carries with him a sort of passive score of True Faith.<br /> <br /> Naturally YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree. The Pope, in his regalia and whatnot, while acting as the Pope, would have the same kind of True Faith say a holy site like the Hagia Sofia has, because of all the people who do actually believe he is God's representative on Earth.<br /> <br /> If you met him one-on-one as Joe Bergoglio, things would be different.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T08:06:02-07:00","id":285921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sarah RPs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/115771-true-faith-seeking?p=279887#post279887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love True Faith, it's one of my favorite merits. To increase it I would prefer that the PC be put in contact with something that challenges their faith. Made it through, even and especially when it was dangerous to hold to your convictions? Cool, have a faith cookie and level up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I let the players have a lot of access to Merits and Flaws in the game I am running, insofar as not limiting the points explicitly. There is a character whom has the True Faith Merit, And the Flaws of Lifesaver, and Icy. There is no decent way of challenging his faith that I can see, because the character has little emotion, and responds to situations as if everything is a bunch of if&gt;then programming.<br /> (I am never allowing &quot;Icy&quot; from the technocracy book, or anything like it, ever again in any RPG. It removes way too much from the 'role' of the 'play'.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}